Thanks for the report. As a work around for now, `X500DistinguishedNameBuilder` encodes this as a PrintableString. In general, this builder offers more flexibility in encoding.

```
using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;

X500DistinguishedNameBuilder builder = new();
builder.AddCountryOrRegion("US");
X500DistinguishedName dn = builder.Build();
Console.WriteLine(Convert.ToBase64String(dn.RawData));
```
